{
  "_comment": "Character classes from the Blade & Sigil design doc. Arrays are indexed by level: index 0 = level 1, index 19 = level 20. SPELL POINTS (magic v2, doc formula): casters use \"spell_points\": {\"base\": N, \"multiplier\": M} — max SP = base + (level x multiplier x 3), so a Wizard (4, 1.0) has 7 SP at level 1 and 64 at level 20. A legacy per-level array still works; classes with neither have no magic. hit_bonus applies to attack AND damage rolls. GEAR: 'starting_weapon' is an item id from items.json. 'weapon_types' lists the weapon categories the class may wield (or [\"any\"]); 'armor_types' lists light/med/heavy; 'shields' allows a shield. These enforce the design doc's item rules. 'detect': per-level % chance (design doc tables, thief & archer) to notice secret doors and traps — the party uses its best detector, +5% per point of DEX modifier, +race detect_bonus. 'disarms': true lets the class defuse a DETECTED trap by stepping onto it (thieves only, per the doc). | \"locked\": true hides a class from character creation until its progression lanes are built (2026-08-26: archer/spellblade/summoner wait; delete the flag to release one). | Itemization v2: 'robe' in armor_types is the armor_robe category (scholar's robes) — every class wears them, including mages. | MAGIC v3 (2026-08-28): 'caster': arcane | divine says which school a class works in — ARCANE casters may READ scrolls in battle. A 'spellbook' block makes the class keep a spellbook FROM LEVEL 1: 'starting_spells' (the kit every new hero opens with), 'study_levels' (each listed level grants one free STUDY pick of any common class spell of castable level — arrives as a card on the map), 'slots_base' (+ max spell level + one per 'extra_slot_levels' reached = prepared spells at a time). 'revelation_levels' (priests): {spell level: character level} — the RARE prayers of that level are revealed automatically on reaching it.",
